course: dictionary
lesson: 15220
title: Sequels and what comes next
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A sequel is a book, film or game that carries on the story of an earlier one. The word sounds like "follow", and that is a clue: a sequel follows after the first story.
explain: «The second book is a sequel to the first.» The first book comes before, and the second one continues the same story with the same characters.
explain: Sequel can also mean something that happens after, and because of, an earlier event. «The flooded streets were a sequel to a week of heavy rain.» The rain came first, and the flooding was the result.
explain: The opposite idea is a prequel, which tells what happened before. Listen for the phrases «a sequel to» and «the long-awaited sequel», which show that something follows on from something else.
fact: A sequel continues the story of an earlier book, film or game.
fact: «Sequel» can also mean something that happens after, and because of, an earlier event.
fact: A prequel is the opposite of a sequel: it tells what happened before.
fact: In English lessons, you might write a sequel to a story you have read, keeping the same characters.
fact: Useful phrases are «a sequel to» and «the long-awaited sequel».
exercise: «The second book is a sequel to the first.» What is a sequel? | A story that tells what happened before | A short poem about the sea | A word for a very small book | *A story that carries on from an earlier one
exercise: Which word means a story that tells what happened before the first one? | summary | *prequel | chapter | sequel
exercise: «The flooded streets were a sequel to a week of heavy rain.» What does sequel suggest here? | A type of weather forecast | *Something that happened after, and because of, the rain | Something that happened before the rain | A kind of boat
test: «Our class wrote a sequel to the story we read, with the same hero.» What did the class write? | A list of new words | A poem about a dragon | A story that comes before the one they read | *A story that carries on from the one they read, with the same hero
test: Which word fits the gap? «The game was a ___ to the one we loved last year.» | *sequel | chapter | summary | prequel
exam: «The sequel to the film was not as good as the first, but the fans still loved the ending.» Why is the film called a sequel? | Because it was made before the first film | *Because it carries on the story of the first film | Because it is shorter than the first | Because it has no characters
